        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n    \"workspaceId\": \"{{workspaceId}}\"\n}\n\n// Use the following request body to migrate an API Builder definition into a new workspace:\n// {\n//    \"workspaceInfo\": {\n//        \"name\": \"{{workspaceName}}\"\n//   }\n//}\n\n// Use the following request body to migrate a Git-connected API Builder definition into a new workspace:\n//{\n//    \"workspaceInfo\": {\n//        \"name\": \"{{workspaceName}}\"\n//    },\n//    \"gitInfo\": {\n//        \"path\": \"{{gitPath}}\"\n//    }\n//}",
          "options": {
            "raw": {
              "language": "json"
            }
          }
        },
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/apis/:apiId/spec-migrations",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "apis",
            ":apiId",
            "spec-migrations"
          ],
          "variable": [
            {
              "key": "apiId",
              "value": "{{apiId}}"
            }
          ]
        },
        "description": "Initiates a migration of an API from API Builder to Spec Hub. This endpoint triggers the migration process for a specified API, moving it to the new Spec Hub architecture within a target workspace.\n\n## Path Variables\n\n| Variable | Type | Required | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `apiId` | string (UUID) | Yes | The unique identifier of the API to migrate from API Builder |\n\n## Headers\n\n| Header | Value | Required | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `Accept` | `application/vnd.api.v10+json` | Yes | Specifies the API version for the response format |\n\n## Request Body\n\n#### Migrate to an existing workspace\n\n``` json\n{\n  \"workspaceId\": \"03dce2f4-89f5-4344-9b85-18a0f13f9f86\"\n}\n\n ```\n\n| Field | Type | Required | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `workspaceId` | string (UUID) | Yes | The target workspace ID where the migrated API will be placed in Spec Hub. |\n\n#### Migrate to a new workspace\n\n``` json\n{\n    \"workspaceInfo\": {\n        \"name\": \"{{workspaceName}}\"\n    },\n    \"gitInfo\": {\n       \"path\": \"{{gitPath}}\"\n    }\n}\n\n ```\n\n| **Field** | **Type** | **Required** | **Description** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `workspaceInfo` | object | Yes | The target workspace ID where the migrated API will be placed in Spec Hub. |\n| `gitInfo` | object |  | Contains info about the connected remote Git repository. |\n| `gitInfo.path` | string |  | The directory path in the remote repository containing the API's collections and definitions. This property expects an absolute path and only contains alphanumeric characters, slashes, hyphens, underscores, and periods. It cannot contain path traversal sequences (`\\..\\`). |\n\n## Usage Notes\n\n- The migration is an asynchronous operation. After initiating the migration, use the [Get migration status](https://request/12420868-879eac37-ddcb-4f81-927e-7bff567b1441) endpoint (GET request to the same path) to check the progress and completion status.\n    \n- Ensure the target `workspaceId` exists and you have appropriate permissions to create resources in that workspace.\n    \n- The original API in API Builder remains unchanged until the migration completes successfully.\n    \n- This endpoint is part of the transition from the legacy API Builder to the newer Spec Hub architecture."
      },
